OL,3,A'The city is alive': A brief peace in
OL,4,AKherson, but residents fear what comes
OL,5,Anext
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe Ukrainian city of Kherson has known
OL,8,Fits first two days of quiet after many
OL,9,Fyears, as a US-brokered temporary
OL,10,Fceasefire has allowed residents rare
OL,11,Fmoments of respite from the constant
OL,12,FRussian aerial attacks that plague the
OL,13,Ffront line region.
OL,15,FVideos posted on social media showed
OL,16,Fpeople strolling down streets covered
OL,17,Fin anti-drone nets and gathering in the
OL,18,Fcity's squares - ordinary activities
OL,19,Fthat usually mean keeping one eye on
OL,20,Fthe sky and one ear out for incoming
OL,21,Fdrones.
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/40
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11913
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1793330305
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,A'The city is alive': A brief peace in
OL,4,AKherson, but residents fear what comes
OL,5,Anext
OL,6,
OL,7,F"Ever since the ceasefire was
OL,8,Fannounced, there's been total silence,"
OL,9,Fsaid Olga, 42, speaking by phone from
OL,10,FKherson. "We are all, of course,
OL,11,Foverjoyed."
OL,13,F"I don't even know what to call it,"
OL,14,Fshe added, her smile coming through in
OL,15,Fher voice. "It's as if everything has
OL,16,Ffinally come to an end."
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/40
